<title>USA: CSCE to raise margins on cocoa futures.</title>
<headline>CSCE to raise margins on cocoa futures.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coffee, Sugar and Cocoa Exchange Inc said Monday it will raise margins on its May 1997 and July 1997 cocoa contracts by $100, to $800, effective April 8.</p>
<p>The margin on all other cocoa contracts will be also be increased by $100 to $800, the exchange said in a statement.</p>
<p>For customers who are not exchange members or a member of the trade, margins will be 140 percent above trade rates, CSCE said.</p>
<p>((--Patricia Avidan, New York Commodities Desk, 212 859 1640))</p>
